  "summary": "Eight preprints link predicted and observed regulatory variant effects to cell states, tissues and ancestry, from AlphaGenome 2 to T2D effector-gene prioritization.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is placing regulatory variant effects in specific cellular, tissue and genetic contexts. AlphaGenome 2 predicts cell-type-specific regulatory activity and variant effects from 1-Mb sequence, and ChromBPNet models of 17 hematopoietic types score 302,830 variants with lineage-structured accessibility effects. Admixed whole-blood RNA-seq links West African ancestry to more allele-specific expression, with 52 ancestry-associated loci replicating. Downstream, CAS-X integrates fine-mapped eQTLs across five metabolic tissues and CELL-X uses islet single-cell transcriptomes for type 2 diabetes. PrediXSKAT weights coding variants by predicted cis-regulated expression. The endometriosis study shows cell-state prioritization depends on marker definition and donor structure. The midkine Mendelian randomization study in pancreatic cancer is only loosely related.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
